You can achieve this by using the pgfplots package in LaTeX. Here is an example code snippet that reads the y-coordinates from a file named "data" where each coordinate is on a new line and the x-coordinates are incrementing at each line:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{pgfplots}
\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}
\begin{axis}
\addplot table {data};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
\end{document}
```

Make sure to have your data file named "data" with the y-coordinates on each line. The x-coordinates will be automatically generated as integers starting from 1.

